      "extract": "The idea of the \\emph{formal deformation quantization} program \\cite{BFFLS}, initiated by Bayen, Flato, Fronsdal, Lichnerowicz and Sternheimer, is to generalize the Weyl product to an arbitrary symplectic (or Poisson) manifold. In this context, the framework of quantum mechanics is the same as classical mechanics, observables are the same, and quantization arises as a \\emph{deformation} of the algebra of functions",
      "extractCut": true
